  "answer they must agree on. The engine draws the chart off a cell; the browser says, in the cell, what",
  "the chart will draw. A cell they read differently is a cell the analyst is told one thing about and",
  "shown another. Read by tests/test_cellread.py and lib/cellRead.test.js.",
  "days: `reads` is the day, its precision and whether the cell said its year; a cell without one is",
  "placed in 2000 (NO_YEAR). null is a cell that is not a day.",
  "numbers: `value` is the number, signed; null when the cell holds no single number (a range, words,",
  "a day). `floor` is a number said as a minimum. `decimal` is the mark the column says, when it says one.",
  "columns: a column's cells read together, its decimal mark said by the cells themselves."
